    "summary": "FFmpeg versions from 0.5 up to, but not including, 9.0 contain a signed integer overflow...",
    "details": "FFmpeg versions from 0.5 up to, but not including, 9.0 contain a signed integer overflow vulnerability in the DVB subtitle parser in `libavcodec/dvbsub_parser.c` that allows attackers to trigger a heap buffer overflow by supplying a crafted WTV file. The overflow causes the bounds-check guard expression to wrap to `INT_MIN`, bypassing the `PARSE_BUF_SIZE` comparison and invoking memcpy() with attacker-controlled data into a heap buffer, resulting in an out-of-bounds heap write and potential memory corruption or code execution.",
    "severity": [
